   "id": "hello-world-markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Hello World - Your First Angular Component
",
    "
",
    "Angular is a TypeScript-based framework for building web applications. Components are the building blocks of Angular apps.
",
    "Each component has a TypeScript class decorated with `@Component` and a template.
"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "hello-world-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import { Component } from '@angular/core';
",
    "
",
    "@Component({
",
    "  selector: 'app-hello-world',
",
    "  template: `<h1>Hello, Angular world!</h1>`
",
    "})
",
    "export class HelloWorldComponent {
",
    "  constructor() {
",
    "    console.log('HelloWorldComponent created');
",
    "  }
",
    "}
"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "interpolation-markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. String Interpolation and Property Binding
",
    "
",
    "Use double curly braces `{{ }}` for string interpolation to display component properties in the template.
",
    "Property binding with `[property]` binds component data to element properties.
"
   ]
  },
